            "output": "<path>/workspace/deps/verifier/src/se/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \n2: # KBS with IBM SE verifier\n3: \n4: This is a document to guide developer run a KBS with IBM SE verifier locally for development purpose.\n5: \n6: ## Index\n7: \n8: - [Deployment of KBS with IBM SE verifier](#deployment-of-kbs-with-ibm-se-verifier)\n9: - [Set attestation policy for IBM SE verifier](#set-attestation-policy)\n10: \n11: \n12: \n13: # Deployment of KBS with IBM SE verifier\n14: \n15: This section is about deployment of KBS without rvps checking.\n16: \n17: ## Generate RSA keys\n18: Generate RSA 4096 key pair following commands:\n19: ```bash\n20: openssl genrsa -aes256 -passout pass:test1234 -out encrypt_key-psw.pem 4096\n21: openssl rsa -in encrypt_key-psw.pem -passin pass:test1234 -pubout -out encrypt_key.pub\n22: openssl rsa -in encrypt_key-psw.pem -out encrypt_key.pem\n23: ```\n24: \n25: \n26: ## Download Certs, CRLs\n27: Donwload these materials from: https://www.ibm.com/support/resourcelink/api/content/public/secure-execution-gen2.html\n28: Which includes:\n29: \n30: ### Certs\n31: ibm-z-host-key-signing-gen2.crt\n32: DigiCertCA.crt \n33: \n34: ### CRL\n35: ibm-z-host-key-gen2.crl  \n36: DigiCertTrustedRootG4.crl  \n37: DigiCertTrustedG4CodeSigningRSA4096SHA3842021CA1.crl\n38: \n39: Note: `DigiCertTrustedRootG4.crl` and `DigiCertTrustedG4CodeSigningRSA4096SHA3842021CA1.crl` come from commands as below:\n40: ```bash\n41: # openssl x509 -in DigiCertCA.crt --text --noout |grep crl\n42:                   URI:http://crl3.digicert.com/DigiCertTrustedRootG4.crl\n43: # openssl x509 -in ibm-z-host-key-signing-gen2.crt --text --noout |grep crl\n44:                   URI:http://crl3.digicert.com/DigiCertTrustedG4CodeSigningRSA4096SHA3842021CA1.crl\n45:                   URI:http://crl4.digicert.com/DigiCertTrustedG4CodeSigningRSA4096SHA3842021CA1.crl\n46: ```\n47: \n48: ## Download HKD\n49: Download IBM Secure Execution Host Key Document following: https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/linux-on-z?topic=execution-verify-host-key-document\n50: \n51: ## Get SE Header\n52: Build `se.img` following [Generate an IBM Secure Execution image](https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/linux-on-systems?topic=commands-genprotimg) and retrieve the hdr.bin via command like below.\n53: ```bash\n54: ./pvextract-hdr -o hdr.bin se.img\n55: ```\n56: \n57: Refer [ibm-s390-linux](https://github.com/ibm-s390-linux/s390-tools/blob/v2.33.1/rust/pvattest/tools/pvextract-hdr) to get `pvextract-hdr`.\n58: \n59: ## Generate KBS key\n60: Generate keys used by KBS service.\n61: ```bash\n62: openssl genpkey -algorithm ed25519 > kbs.key\n63: openssl pkey -in kbs.key -pubout -out kbs.pem\n64: ```\n65: \n66: ## (Option 1) Launch KBS as a program\n67: \n68: - Build KBS\n69: ```bash\n70: cargo install --locked --debug --path kbs/src/kbs --no-default-features --features coco-as-builtin,openssl,resource,opa \n71: ```\n72: \n73: - Prepare the material retrieved above, similar as:\n74: ```\n75: /run/confidential-containers/ibmse#\n76: .\n77: ├── certs\n78: │   ├── ibm-z-host-key-signing-gen2.crt\n79: |   └── DigiCertCA.crt\n80: ├── crls\n81: │   └── ibm-z-host-key-gen2.crl\n82: │   └── DigiCertTrustedRootG4.crl\n83: │   └── DigiCertTrustedG4CodeSigningRSA4096SHA3842021CA1.crl\n84: ├── hdr\n85: │   └── hdr.bin\n86: ├── hkds\n87: │   └── HKD-3931-0275D38.crt\n88: └── rsa\n89:     ├── encrypt_key.pem\n90:     └── encrypt_key.pub\n91: ```\n92: \n93: > Note: alternative is to use system variables listed in [ibmse.rs](./ibmse.rs) to overwrite the files.\n94: \n95: - Prepare the `kbs-config.toml`, similar as:\n96: ```\n97: sockets = [\"0.0.0.0:8080\"]\n98: auth_public_key = \"/kbs/kbs.pem\"\n99: # Ideally we should use some solution like cert-manager to issue let's encrypt based certificate:\n100: # https://cert-manager.io/docs/configuration/acme/\n101: insecure_http = true\n102: \n103: [attestation_token_config]\n104: attestation_token_type = \"CoCo\"\n105: \n106: [as_config]\n107: work_dir = \"/opt/confidential-containers/attestation-service\"\n108: policy_engine = \"opa\"\n109: attestation_token_broker = \"Simple\"\n110: \n111: [as_config.attestation_token_config]\n112: duration_min = 5\n113: \n114: [as_config.rvps_config]\n115: store_type = \"LocalFs\"\n116: remote_addr = \"\"\n117: ```\n118: \n119: - Launch the KBS program\n120: ```bash\n121: export RUST_LOG=debug\n122: export SE_SKIP_CERTS_VERIFICATION=true\n123: ./kbs --config-file ./kbs-config.toml\n124: ```\n125: \n126: > Note: `export SE_SKIP_CERTS_VERIFICATION=true` only required for a development machine. Use `export CERTS_OFFLINE_VERIFICATION=true` to verifiy the certificates offline.\n127: \n128: ## (Option 2) Launch KBS via docker-compose\n129: - Build the docker image\n130: ```\n131: DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 docker build --build-arg HTTPS_CRYPTO=\"openssl\" --build-arg ARCH=\"s390x\" -t ghcr.io/confidential-containers/staged-images/kbs:latest . -f kbs/docker/Dockerfile\n132: ```\n133: >Note: Please add `--debug` in statement like `cargo install` in file `kbs/docker/Dockerfile` if you're using a development host key document to skip HKD's signature verification.\n134: \n135: - Prepare a docker compose file, similar as:\n136: ```\n137: services:\n138:   kbs:\n139:     image: ghcr.io/confidential-containers/staged-images/kbs:latest\n140:     command: [\n141:         \"/usr/local/bin/kbs\",\n142:         \"--config-file\",\n143:         \"/etc/kbs-config.toml\",\n144:       ]\n145:     restart: always # keep the server running\n146:     environment:\n147:       - RUST_LOG=debug\n148:       - SE_SKIP_CERTS_VERIFICATION=true\n149:     ports:\n150:       - \"8080:8080\"\n151:     volumes:\n152:       - ./data/kbs-storage:/opt/confidential-containers/kbs/repository:rw\n153:       - ./data/attestation-service:/opt/confidential-containers/attestation-service:rw\n154:       - ./kbs.pem:/kbs/kbs.pem\n155:       - ./kbs-config.toml:/etc/kbs-config.toml\n156:       - ./data/hkds:/run/confidential-containers/ibmse/hkds\n157:       - ./data/certs:/run/confidential-containers/ibmse/certs\n158:       - ./data/crls:/run/confidential-containers/ibmse/crls\n159:       - ./data/hdr.bin:/run/confidential-containers/ibmse/hdr/hdr.bin\n160:       - ./data/rsa/encrypt_key.pem:/run/confidential-containers/ibmse/rsa/encrypt_key.pem\n161:       - ./data/rsa/encrypt_key.pub:/run/confidential-containers/ibmse/rsa/encrypt_key.pub\n162: ```\n163: > Note: `export SE_SKIP_CERTS_VERIFICATION=true` only required for a development machine. Use `export CERTS_OFFLINE_VERIFICATION=true` to verifiy the certificates offline.\n164: \n165: - Prepare the material, similar as:\n166: ```\n167: .\n168: ├── data\n169: │   ├── attestation-service\n170: │   │   ├── opa\n171: │   │   │   └── default.rego\n172: │   ├── certs\n173: │   │   ├── ibm-z-host-key-signing-gen2.crt\n174: │   │   └── DigiCertCA.crt\n175: │   ├── crls\n176: │   │   └── ibm-z-host-key-gen2.crl\n177: │   │   └── DigiCertTrustedRootG4.crl\n178: │   │   └── DigiCertTrustedG4CodeSigningRSA4096SHA3842021CA1.crl\n179: │   ├── hdr.bin\n180: │   ├── hkds\n181: │   │   └── HKD-3931-0275D38.crt\n182: │   ├── kbs-storage\n183: │   │   ├── default\n184: │   │   └── one\n185: │   │       └── two\n186: │   │           └── key\n187: │   └── rsa\n188: │       ├── encrypt_key.pem\n189: │       └── encrypt_key.pub\n190: ├── docker-compose.yaml\n191: ├── kbs-config.toml\n192: ├── kbs.key\n193: └── kbs.pem\n194: ```\n195: \n196: - Launch KBS as docker compose application\n197: ```bash\n198: docker-compose up -d\n199: docker-compose logs kbs\n200: docker-compose down\n201: ```\n202: \n203: \n204: # Set attestation policy\n205: \n206: This section is about setting attestation policy.\n207: \n208: ### Retrive the attestation policy fields for IBM SE\n209: \n210: Using [se_parse_hdr.py](se_parse_hdr.py) on a s390x instance to retrieve the IBM SE fields for attestation policy.\n211: \n212: ```bash\n213: python3 se_parse_hdr.py hdr.bin HKD-3931.crt \n214: \n215: ...\n216:   ================================================ \n217:   se.image_phkh: xxx\n218:   se.version: 256\n219:   se.tag: xxx\n220:   se.attestation_phkh: xxx\n221: ```\n222: \n223: We get following fields and will set these fields in rvps for attestation policy. \n224: `se.version: 256`  \n225: `se.tag: xxx`  \n226: `se.attestation_phkh: xxx`  \n227: `se.image_phkh: xxx`  \n228: \n229: \n230: ### Set attestation policy\n231: \n232: #### Generate attestation policy file\n233: ```bash\n234: cat << EOF > ibmse-policy.rego\n235: package policy\n236: import rego.v1\n237: default allow = false\n238: \n239: converted_version := sprintf(\"%v\", [input[\"se.version\"]])\n240: \n241: allow if {\n242:     input[\"se.attestation_phkh\"] == \"xxx\"\n243:     input[\"se.image_phkh\"] == \"xxx\"\n244:     input[\"se.tag\"] == \"xxx\"\n245:     input[\"se.user_data\"] == \"00\"\n246:     converted_version == \"256\"\n247: }\n248: EOF\n249: ```\n250: \n251: Where the values come from [retrive-the-rvps-field-for-an-ibm-se-image](#retrive-the-rvps-field-for-an-ibm-se-image)\n252: \n253: #### Set the attestation policy\n254: ```bash\n255: kbs-client --url http://127.0.0.1:8080 config --auth-private-key ./kbs/kbs.key set-attestation-policy --policy-file ./ibmse-policy.rego\n256: ```\n\n(End of file - total 256 lines)\n</content>",
